<main class="write-main"><h1>Footer visitor statistics</h1><?php foreach(flashes()as$f):?><p class="notice" role="status"><?=e($f['message'])?></p><?php endforeach;?><?php if($error):?><p class="notice error" role="alert"><?=e($error)?></p><?php endif;?>
<section class="settings-card"><h2>Verified Google Analytics aggregates</h2><p>Status: <?=e($statistics['status']??'Not refreshed')?>. <a href="<?=url('/write/google#diagnostics')?>">Google diagnostics</a></p><p>Active visitors measures consented activity during the last 30 minutes, not an exact count of people online now. Recorded visits are GA4 sessions since the selected web stream’s creation date. Repeated sessions can belong to the same person; consent choices, blockers and processing affect totals. No earlier site history is invented.</p><p>The worker refreshes recent activity about once a minute and totals hourly. Stale or missing readings show as unavailable, never a fabricated zero. Only the verified stream matching this website’s deployed tag is used; the public footer never calls Google directly.</p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn primary">Refresh verified statistics</button></form><p>Recorded visits: <?=isset($statistics['visits'])?number_format($statistics['visits']):'Unavailable'?> · Since: <?=e($statistics['since']??'Unavailable')?></p></section></main>
